[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"lane_gib"
text = "# DRAFT
# Gib the watchman lighting the lanterns along the lane at dusk, nights 1 to 6.
# After a lane death he's the one who found the body or heard the cry. He always reminds the porter of the bell.
# His own flags: lane_gib_<night> (talked to him tonight), lane_gib_n<night>_<topic> (asked).
== start
-> start_known [if talked_n0_gib]
-> start_new

== start_known
Gib: Brother. Still in one piece. Good.
-> tonight

== start_new
(An old man on a short ladder, coaxing a lantern alight.)
Gib: Gib, the watch. Mind my ladder, brother.
-> tonight

== again
-> back [if night=1] [if lane_gib_1]
-> back [if night=2] [if lane_gib_2]
-> back [if night=3] [if lane_gib_3]
-> back [if night=4] [if lane_gib_4]
-> back [if night=5] [if lane_gib_5]
-> back [if night=6] [if lane_gib_6]
-> hello

== hello
Gib: Brother.
-> tonight

== back
Gib: Still here? I've lanterns to light.
-> ask

== tonight
-> n1 [if night=1]
-> n2 [if night=2]
-> n3 [if night=3]
-> n4 [if night=4]
-> n5 [if night=5]
-> n6 [if night=6]

== ask
-> n1_ask [if night=1]
-> n2_ask [if night=2]
-> n3_ask [if night=3]
-> n4_ask [if night=4]
-> n5_ask [if night=5]
-> n6_ask [if night=6]

# Night 1: night 0's killing was behind the wall. He heard something.
== n1 [set lane_gib_1]
Gib: Quiet night, last night. Quiet as I like it. Bar a fox crying over your wall, round midnight.
-> n1_ask

== n1_ask
* [if not lane_gib_n1_fox] A fox? -> n1_fox
* [if not lane_gib_n1_hour] When do you start calling? -> n1_hour

== n1_fox [set lane_gib_n1_fox]
Gib: Must have been. What else cries like that, at that hour?
(He goes up his ladder and doesn't look down.)
-> n1_ask

== n1_hour [set lane_gib_n1_hour]
Gib: At the bell. Nine, and then every hour till the light.
Gib: You'll hear me from your gate. Listen for me, brother.
-> n1_ask

# Night 2
== n2 [set lane_gib_2]
Gib: Rain again. Keeps the lanterns spitting.
Gib: After the bell there's nobody in this lane but me. Nobody should be.
-> n2_ask

== n2_ask
* [if not lane_gib_n2_out] What if someone's out after the bell? -> n2_out

== n2_out [set lane_gib_n2_out]
Gib: Then I tell him to get indoors, and I walk on. I'm one old man with a lantern, brother.
Gib: Send them to the Keys while the Keys is open.
-> n2_ask

# Night 3: about night 2. He found the body in the lane, or something passed him.
== n3 [set lane_gib_3]
-> n3_jankin [if died_jankin]
-> n3_turned [if died_lane_death] [if lane_death_was_turned_away]
-> n3_other [if died_lane_death]
-> n3_passed

== n3_jankin
Gib: It was me found Jankin. Two o'clock, in the gutter by the chandler's.
Gib: I called the hour and he didn't answer. He always answered. Is it, Gib, he'd say. Is it all well?
(The taper shakes in his hand, and he has to light it again.)
-> n3_bell

== n3_turned
Gib: It was me found him. The poor soul who was turned off at your gate after the bell.
Gib: In the gutter, under my own lantern. I heard him cry out, and I was three houses off. Three houses.
-> n3_bell

== n3_other
Gib: It was me found him, in the gutter under my own lantern. I heard him cry out. I was three houses off.
-> n3_bell

== n3_passed
Gib: Something went past me last night, at three. Close as you are now.
Gib: I never saw it. I smelled it. Like a church.
-> n3_bell

== n3_bell
Gib: Bell's at nine. Be behind your gate when it goes, and keep it barred.
-> n3_ask

== n3_ask
* [if not lane_gib_n3_walk] Will you still walk the lane tonight? -> n3_walk

== n3_walk [set lane_gib_n3_walk]
Gib: Mayor pays me to. Every hour, till the light.
Gib: You listen for me, brother. If I stop calling, I've stopped.
-> n3_ask

# Night 4: about night 3. Running over the wall. Fog coming.
== n4 [set lane_gib_4]
Gib: Fog's coming up off the river. I'll not see one lantern from the next tonight.
Gib: And I heard running over your wall last night. Running, in an abbey, at two in the morning.
-> n4_ask

== n4_ask
* [if not lane_gib_n4_run] It was me. -> n4_me
* [if not lane_gib_n4_run] You must have dreamed it. -> n4_dream

== n4_me [set lane_gib_n4_run]
Gib: Then God help you, brother, whatever it was behind you.
-> n4_ask

== n4_dream [set lane_gib_n4_run]
Gib: I don't sleep on the watch, brother. That's the whole of the job.
-> n4_ask

# Night 5: about night 4. A cry in the fog; Mab's place empty, if she was let in.
== n5 [set lane_gib_5]
-> n5_cry [if died_choira]
-> n5_mab

== n5_cry
Gib: Heard a cry over your wall last night, in the fog. Then nothing.
Gib: I called the hour twice over, to be sure I was still there.
-> n5_mab

== n5_mab
-> n5_empty [if n4_mab=admitted]
-> n5_bell

== n5_empty
Gib: And Mab's place by your gate was empty at midnight. First time in all my years on this lane.
-> n5_bell

== n5_bell
Gib: Bell at nine, brother. Same as ever.
-> n5_ask

== n5_ask
* [if not lane_gib_n5_eye] Keep an eye on my gate tonight. -> n5_eye

== n5_eye [set lane_gib_n5_eye]
Gib: I always do. From the far side of the lane, mind.
-> n5_ask

# Night 6: about night 5. Roger's sergeant, left outside the gate or let in. Snow.
== n6 [set lane_gib_6]
-> n6_dead [if died_sergeant]
-> n6_lived [if n5_sergeant=admitted]
-> n6_snow

== n6_dead
Gib: It was me found the bailiff's man. His lantern out, and him by your gate, where he'd stood all night.
Gib: He'd been calling at your grille. I heard him from the corner. Then he stopped.
-> n6_snow

== n6_lived
Gib: The bailiff's man sat inside your gate all night, they say. Good. That's one I didn't find.
-> n6_snow

== n6_snow
Gib: Snow. You'll see every footprint in the lane tonight. Mine, and whatever else walks it.
Gib: Be behind your gate at the bell, brother. Tonight of all nights.
-> n6_ask

== n6_ask
* [if not lane_gib_n6_call] Call the hour for me tonight. -> n6_call

== n6_call [set lane_gib_n6_call]
Gib: Every hour, till the light. Listen for me.
-> n6_ask

== leave
Gib: Behind your gate at the bell, brother!
"
